592186435548 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435548 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435548 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435548 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435548 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6aa0ef9-33dc-511a-a8b4-7535395d3236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1071 "At which point on the surface $z=4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,1⟩?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0b70f07-48f3-5e91-bb4d-83ea4566f9c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435553 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-4x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨-2,-5,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩=⟨-2,-5,1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4cx &=-2 \\\\ -10cy &=-5 \\\\ -c &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-4(-1)x=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-10(-1)y=-5\\,⟹\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =4-2{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-5{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{4}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186435554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0af89c86-dd82-51d3-8a60-9428fdaf17c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52566cd2-c610-5b7e-a93b-8dfb407f2200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435556 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435556 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8189ee1b-e555-5395-af62-45720087b2f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435556 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435557 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435557 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9be88cd8-1668-517f-a1dd-283be301d1d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435557 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435558 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435558 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a871d925-4e2d-5145-8579-f86cf5c4e2f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435558 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509679 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186510484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186509679 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186510508 #edb/ref 175921